doc('NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT.md','''# Novelty boundary
No established originality claim. Main presentation: Option B, implementation-specific methodological investigation.

| Closest prior contribution | This study actually adds | Boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Mao survey/dynamic offloading: coupled radio/computation, energy causality | Reproducible diagnosis of a preserved negative comparison | No new joint-control theory or battery model.|
| Sun/Dai/Do-Duy: digital-twin offloading, learning/optimization, edge selection | Source-level accounting of what frozen labels enforce | Twin context and edge selection are established.|
| Wang: predicted future local/migration cost and look-ahead | Exact aggregate switching decomposition for frozen actions | No new MPC, horizon optimizer or migration-cost model.|
| Hui: composite-service edge collaboration | Bounded continuous synthetic score analysis | No evaluated vehicular service system.|
| Almohammedi preprint: predictive-fidelity monitors and fallback | Distinction between service-fidelity action and twin prediction fidelity | No comparable accuracy-aware arbitration.|
| Jain index: share allocation fairness | Symmetric allocation objective characterized, primary metric insensitive to share distribution | Fairness formula itself not original; no delivered-service fairness.|

The coherent contribution is preservation plus independent mathematical/statistical characterization: linear-selector collapse and tie boundary, uniform mathematical share optimum with nonzero numerical residuals, unfair consumed-information/action/computation opportunities, truth-changing intervention, negative/inconclusive outcomes. It is useful for skeptical inspection of this archived model; general significance remains for human assessment. No reproduced comparison to published state-of-the-art controllers exists. New evidence would be needed for journal-level efficacy claims. Literature search is targeted, with explicit access gaps; it cannot establish priority or exhaustive novelty.''')
